# Netlify rewrite rules. Copied verbatim into the published site by Docusaurus,
# which treats everything under static/ as a site asset (like _headers beside it).

# PostHog analytics proxy (US region). /ingest is the client's api_host
# (static/analytics.js), so events, remote config and lazily loaded extensions are
# all same-origin, which keeps them working past ad-blockers that filter the
# posthog.com hostnames.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: Netlify applies the first rule that matches, so the two asset
# paths must come before the catch-all, or /ingest/static/* is sent to the API
# host and 404s. 200 makes each a rewrite; the ! forces it even if a file shadows.
/ingest/static/*  https://us-assets.i.posthog.com/static/:splat  200!
/ingest/array/*   https://us-assets.i.posthog.com/array/:splat   200!
/ingest/*         https://us.i.posthog.com/:splat                200!
